# WHAT THE RETIREMENT PUT AT RISK is the dispatcher, and it is a real bug this
# arm found: `_stop-fleet-supervisor` and `_stop-supervisor` were deleted as
# WORDS, and every unmatched word past the dispatcher FALLS THROUGH TO LAUNCH,
# where the last positional is taken as a session name. So this exact command
# silently CREATED a session called `not-a-uuid` (measured — and with a real
# uuid as the op it created a UUID-named session and hung the suite) instead of
# erroring. A retired internal entry must fail closed, not become a launch.
